WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:06.550
No matter how violent, depraved, or overtly
sexual a video game is, rallying the public

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:12.160
in an effort to censor a title will always
bring more attention to the game in question.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.470
If you tell the gaming audience that they
can't play a game, they're going to want to

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.470
play it.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:21.990
"So tell your folks 'Buy me Bonestorm or go
to hell!'"

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:28.150
Here are a few examples when video game censorship
went very wrong.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.180
Death Race

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:34.530
If you think public outrage over video games
is a modern thing, think again.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:40.290
Exidy's Death Race is a 1976 arcade title
in which players zoom around a black and white

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:43.010
screen, running over stick figures to gain
points.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:47.540
Officially, the creatures are "gremlins,"
but there's little difference between a monster

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:51.180
and a normal human being in the space of a
few pixels.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:56.010
Death Race wasn't anything special, but once
the Associated Press ran an article about

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:02.190
it, weirdly comparing the game's digital beeps
to the "scream of a child," it was off to

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:06.370
the digital races.

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:10.750
After that, various articles denounced the
game as "sick" and "morbid," and called for

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.750
its removal from arcades.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:13.750
The end result?

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:21.180
Death Race sold very, very well, and in 1976,
Exidy made $3 million thanks to Death Race

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.180
alone.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:27.040
Exidy released games until 1989, and violent
video games were here to stay.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:31.220
Mortal Kombat

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:36.760
Way back in the early '90s, Nintendo controlled
90 percent of the United States' video game

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:39.890
market… but it had powerful rival.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:45.530
Sega managed to create a unique niche for
itself by promoting their 16-bit Sega Genesis

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:51.300
as a more mature, edgier product than the
Super Nintendo, which was portrayed as family-friendly

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.300
toy.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:57.040
Enter: the notoriously bloody fighting game,
Mortal Kombat.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.960
"Johnny Cage Wins!"

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:06.909
After a successful arcade release, both Nintendo
and Sega had to make a choice when it came

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:10.870
to their console editions: to censor, or not
to censor?

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:16.150
Sega went for blood, albeit in a roundabout
way, with an easy-to-remember cheat code to

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:19.680
unlock the game's gore, but Nintendo kept
it clean.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.680
"Finish her!"

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:30.380
As a result, the Genesis version of Mortal
Kombat sold more copies than its Nintendo

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:33.440
cousin, inadvertently proving Sega's point.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:38.099
The Genesis really was the system to usher
in the next era of gaming.

00:02:38.099 --> 00:02:39.099
Night Trap

00:02:39.099 --> 00:02:45.190
There's only one reason you've heard of Night
Trap, and it's not because the 1992 full-motion

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.980
video game is any good.

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:48.730
'I'm so confused!

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.480
What's going on?"

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:55.120
In 1993, when the United States Senate held
a hearing about the effect of video games

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:01.410
on players, politicians singled out Night
Trap and Mortal Kombat as particularly egregious

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.879
examples of video game violence.

00:03:03.879 --> 00:03:07.910
"The second game is Night Trap, which is a
game set in a sorority house.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:14.050
The object is to keep hooded men from hanging
the young woman with a hook…"

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:18.070
Complaints from parents followed, and Sega
pulled Night Trap from store shelves right

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:21.910
before Christmas, promising to release a censored
version down the line.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:26.989
But instead of keeping the content under wraps,
the Senate hearings boosted the game's profile

00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:28.610
on a national scale.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:33.670
When Night Trap came out for PC and Mac in
1994, Digital Pictures specifically used the

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:35.500
controversy as a selling point.

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.500
The real kicker?

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.530
The ESRB, which was founded as a direct response
to these Senate hearings, rated the upcoming

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:47.010
Night Trap remaster "T for Teen": appropriate
for players 13 and up.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:48.010
Manhunt

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:52.459
Rockstar Games is well-acquainted with controversy,
being the folks behind the Grand Theft Auto

00:03:52.459 --> 00:03:56.701
series and all, but despite critics' claims,
Grand Theft Auto doesn't force you to run

00:03:56.701 --> 00:03:58.480
over hookers or innocent pedestrians.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:03.510
For the most part, the only people that you
have to kill are other criminals.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.400
Rockstar's Manhunt is different.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:10.550
Speaking to GamesRadar, a former Rockstar
employee revealed the game's troubled history,

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:15.030
revealing that company employees threatened
to mutiny because of the game's excessively

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.529
violent content, saying,

00:04:16.529 --> 00:04:20.409
"With GTA, we always had the excuse that the
gameplay was untethered….

00:04:20.409 --> 00:04:23.610
You could play completely ethically if you
wanted."

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:26.490
"Manhunt, though, just made us all feel icky.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:30.259
It was all about the violence, and it was
realistic violence."

00:04:30.259 --> 00:04:33.039
The rest of the world responded similarly.

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:37.800
Politicians introduced legislation to fine
retailers that sold mature games to kids.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:42.990
And after an alleged Manhunt fan murdered
a 14-year-old with a hammer, mimicking one

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:46.949
of Manhunt's grisly kills, some stores pulled
the game entirely.

00:04:46.949 --> 00:04:50.960
When Rockstar decided to press ahead with
an even more depraved sequel, they didn't

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.789
even have to do much marketing.

00:04:52.789 --> 00:04:54.249
As the New York Times noted,

00:04:54.249 --> 00:04:59.740
"Manhunt 2 has received free publicity and
media attention it would have never enjoyed

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:05.020
were it not for the presumably unwitting complicity
of the ratings boards and self-appointed media

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:06.020
watchdogs."

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:07.869
"It is called Manhunt 2.

00:05:07.869 --> 00:05:12.639
And we must warn you, there is nothing about
this that is not disturbing."

00:05:12.639 --> 00:05:13.849
HuniePop

00:05:13.849 --> 00:05:19.460
It's not just violence that attracts censors;
sex is a big problem, too, especially in North

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:20.460
America.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:25.210
Take HuniePop, for example: a game that fuses
match-three puzzles with a visual novel.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:29.479
But it also asks the player to seduce a variety
of anime women.

00:05:29.479 --> 00:05:33.880
Succeed, and you'll not only get down with
your digital lady, but you'll also unlock

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:36.400
some explicit illustrations.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:40.939
Critics begrudgingly agree that it's a good
puzzle game, but at its core, it's pretty

00:05:40.939 --> 00:05:42.879
clearly cartoon porn.

00:05:42.879 --> 00:05:47.879
While HuniePop is right at home among the
visual novels produced in Japan, it's awfully

00:05:47.879 --> 00:05:52.780
racy for mainstream American outlets, and
it's been both banned from Twitch and heavily

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:53.889
censored on Steam.

00:05:53.889 --> 00:06:00.819
But that controversy also generated awareness:
HuniePop moved around 540,000 copies in its

00:06:00.819 --> 00:06:04.240
edit form, which isn't bad for a niche title.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:09.039
Of course, there's a catch: shortly after
HuniePop arrived on Steam, the game's developers

00:06:09.039 --> 00:06:14.369
released a free patch that restored the hidden
content, voiding the Steam-imposed censorship

00:06:14.369 --> 00:06:15.539
after all.

00:06:15.539 --> 00:06:17.060
Point: perverts.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.360
Postal 2

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:22.150
The difference that censorship made for the
Postal franchise is clear.

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:27.020
The first Postal received mediocre reviews
and didn't make much of an impact, aside from

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:30.270
an attempted ban championed by senator Joe
Lieberman.

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:35.449
Its sequel, Postal 2, spawned a feature film
spinoff, broke sales records, and continues

00:06:35.449 --> 00:06:39.729
to receive expansion packs and new content
from its developer, even though the game is

00:06:39.729 --> 00:06:41.479
15 years old.

00:06:41.479 --> 00:06:43.069
So, what changed?

00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:47.270
The New Zealand government succeeded in banning
Postal 2 on the grounds that

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:51.949
"...the game is designed, and has the capacity,
to allow the player to test how much violence

00:06:51.949 --> 00:06:55.490
and humiliation he or she can inflict on human
beings."

00:06:55.490 --> 00:07:00.529
Australia refused to certify the game, effectively
making it illegal in the country.

00:07:00.529 --> 00:07:05.339
The Swedish government tried and failed to
sue Postal 2's local distributor for selling

00:07:05.339 --> 00:07:06.339
violent content.

00:07:06.339 --> 00:07:09.069
All of these things just ended up promoting
the game.

00:07:09.069 --> 00:07:14.319
Postal 2 even received an expansion pack in
2015, and a modern remaster of the first game

00:07:14.319 --> 00:07:16.020
arrived in 2016.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:21.159
Plans for Postal 4 are reportedly under way—and,
if history is any indication, it'll freak

00:07:21.159 --> 00:07:22.789
out people all over again.

00:07:22.789 --> 00:07:23.789
Thanks for watching!

